$\begin{aligned}
& f\left(x_1\right)-f\left(x_2\right)=f\left(\frac{x_1-x_2}{1-x_1 x_2}\right) \\
& x_1, x_2 \in(-1,1)
\end{aligned}$
then $f(x)=\log \frac{(1-x)}{(1+x)}\begin{gathered}
f\left(x_1\right)=\log \frac{1-x_1}{1+x_1} \quad f\left(x_2\right)=\log \frac{1-x_2}{1+x_2} \\
\begin{aligned}
f\left(x_1\right)-f\left(x_2\right) & =\log \frac{1-x_1}{1+x_1}-\log \frac{1-x_2}{1+x_2} \\
& =\log \frac{\left(1-x_1\right)}{\left(1+x_1\right)} \times \frac{\left(1+x_2\right)}{\left(1-x_2\right)} \\
= & \log \frac{\left(1-x_1+x_2-x_1 x_2\right)}{\left(1+x_1-x_2-x_1 x_2\right)} \\
= & \log \frac{\left(1-x_1 x_2\right)-\left(x_1-x_2\right)}{\left(1-x_1 x_2\right)+\left(x_1-x_2\right)}
\end{aligned}\end{gathered}=\log \frac{1-\left(\frac{x_1-x_2}{1-x_1 x_2}\right)}{1+\left(\frac{x_1-x_2}{1-x_1 x_2}\right)}f\left(x_1\right)-f\left(x_2\right)=f\left(\frac{x_1-x_2}{1-x_1 x_2}\right)$

$\begin{aligned} & \text { Let }[A]=\left[\begin{array}{ll}a & b \\ c & d\end{array}\right] \\ & \begin{aligned} A^{-1} & =\frac{1}{|A|}(a d j . A) \\ & =\frac{1}{(a d-b c)}\left[\begin{array}{cc}d & -c \\ -b & a\end{array}\right]^T=\frac{1}{(a d-b c)}\left[\begin{array}{cc}d & -b \\ -c & a\end{array}\right]\end{aligned}\end{aligned}\begin{aligned}
& \operatorname{adj}\left(A^{-1}\right)=\frac{1}{(a d-b c)}\left[\begin{array}{ll}
a & c \\
b & d
\end{array}\right]^T=\frac{1}{(a d-b c)}\left[\begin{array}{ll}
a & b \\
c & d
\end{array}\right]...(1) \\
& \operatorname{adj} A=\left[\begin{array}{cc}
d & -b \\
-c & a
\end{array}\right] \\
& |\operatorname{adj} A|=(a d-b c) \\
& (\operatorname{adj} A)^{-1}=\frac{1}{\mid a d j} A \left\lvert\,\left[\begin{array}{ll}
a & c \\
b & d
\end{array}\right]^T=\frac{1}{a d-b c}\left[\begin{array}{ll}
